# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MOST IMPORTANT FILE IN THIS REPO -- and as of 2026-08-25, one rule.
#
# Everything about, belonging to, or specific to a user lives under vault/.
# Nothing else in this repository is theirs. That is the whole boundary, and it
# is what makes an update possible: the system outside vault/ can be replaced
# wholesale without touching a year of somebody's working life.
#
# WHY THIS USED TO BE COMPLICATED, AND WHY THAT MATTERED
#
# There were eight rules, because user data sat inside tools/. One of them,
# `tools/radar/*.json`, silently swallowed TWO files that had to ship -- an
# example config and the ATS registry -- and each was found only because someone
# noticed a clone was broken. The carve-outs that fixed them were `!` lines
# added one filename at a time, and the next file into that directory would have
# been swallowed too.
#
# One rule cannot do that. If something is the user's, it goes in vault/. If it
# is not, it ships. There is no third case and no list to maintain.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

vault/

# tools/tests/test_boundary.py fails the build if user data appears outside
# vault/, or if anything under vault/ is tracked. The rule above is the
# intention; that test is the enforcement.

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
